    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "43892d97bb179bf2df84dcb0b8d22500",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"differential-equations-from-ibp\">Differential equations from IBP</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_bubble.py\">Bubble reductions</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/ibp_triangle.py\">Massless triangle</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Differentiating a loop integral produces raised propagator powers. IBP\nreduces these derivatives to the original basis, giving differential\nequations for the master integrals. This notebook composes the\nunequal-mass bubble notebook, reusing its family and reductions.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_1=k^2-a||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D_2=(k-p)^2-b||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(p^2=s||)</marimo-tex>, define the vector\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mathbf J=(A(a),A(b),B(s,a,b))^T=(I(1,0),I(0,1),I(1,1))^T||)</marimo-tex>.\nThe three equations are <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\partial_v\\mathbf J=M_v\\mathbf J||)</marimo-tex>,\nfor <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(v=s,a,b||)</marimo-tex>. Symbolica checks their compatibility exactly; then a\nnumerical solution transports one boundary value to another invariant.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
